Java springboot : Springboot related information stored in POM.xml file (Project Object Model)
Springboot is a java framework if you want to develop web based app. Dev will write in pom.xml
POM.xml is a configuration file can also be used other then springboot.

Maven : Build automation tool for java.

Springboot app :
developer write the code and give you the link to git repo
you run the maven commands to build it :
mvn clean : delete old compiled files target/folder
mvn test : run all test cases imp in prod
mvn package: compiles code + run tests + create JAR file

Behind the scene : 
java code is compiled to .class file
Dependencies springboot,etc are auto downloaded via Maven(pom.xml)
final output : executable.jar
then you run the app : 
    #java -jar appname.jar --httpPort=8082 #anyport
-----------------
Now go to jenkins 
create freestyle project > configure > add git repo of the springboot app > change master branch to main branch
build will be a SUCCESS because integration of git and jenkins is successful, not because the java code is OK.
ADD BUILD STEPS in shell :
  -  mvn test
  -  mvn package
  build again > it will give mvn not found error
  Now , we have to install maven on the jenkins server by ssh into jenkins server.
     # apt-get install maven
  again build and now build will be successful
  Check for target directory path from project name > workspace > target/package.jar 
  SSH into jenkins server and go to above path and run command:
      # java -jar shopping_Cart.jar --httpPort=3000
    
